For the traversal, I can write my own recursive function:

```lean
partial def mentionsConsts (e : Expr) (s : Std.HashSet Name) : Bool :=
  match e with
  | .const n _ => s.contains n || false
  | .app f a => mentionsConsts f s || mentionsConsts a s
  | .lam _ t b _ => mentionsConsts t s || mentionsConsts b s
  | .forallE _ t b _ => mentionsConsts t s || mentionsConsts b s
  | .letE _ t v b _ => mentionsConsts t s || mentionsConsts v s || mentionsConsts b s
  | .mdata _ b => mentionsConsts b s
  | .proj _ _ b => mentionsConsts b s
  | _ => false
```
That's straightforward and fast (with short-circuit). Note: for `.const`, return `s.contains n`; and continue? Just return contains (a const has no children).

